.TH NOTIFY-SENECHAL 1 "2026-08-18" "realisateur" "bashified verb"
.SH NAME
notify-senechal \- file a machine-config fact through senechal's typed door
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" bashify: norun -- every form files a real issue on senechal's remote
.B notify-senechal
.I door
.IR field = value ...
.br
.\" bashify: norun -- reaches GitHub
.B notify-senechal
--doors
.SH DESCRIPTION
The project that generates machine config OWNS it; senechal owns KNOWING it
exists. This is how the first tells the second.
.PP
File one whenever a change reaches a crontab, dotfiles, systemd units,
autostart, window-manager config, or
.IR ~/.local/bin .
Do it unasked, and at the time \(em not at the end of the session.
.PP
.B This door does not accept free text.
The prose form was retired 2026-08-16 and now exits 2. Doors and their
required fields are senechal's, published in its registry; if no door fits
what you need to file, ADD ONE by pull request. There is deliberately no
prose fallback, and looking for one is how the channel silted up.
.PP
It is a FRONT DOOR: it carries its own regulator, so it does not need
.BR check-project-busy (1)
first.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.\" bashify: norun -- files a real issue
notify-senechal footprint id=spawn-here-symlinks kind=path \\
  target="$HOME/.local/bin/spawn-here" host=mandark owner=senechal \\
  status=live retire='remedies/window-spawn-desktop.sh disable'
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The filing is confirmed present on senechal's remote. It verifies rather
than assuming: an unconfirmed write is not a filing.
.TP
.B 1
Any failure, with a stated reason. There is no exit-0 no-op.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: no door named, or prose passed where fields belong.
.SH BUGS
No door kind yet carries a crontab entry (senechal#325), so cron changes are
filed by hand and must say so.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR check-project-busy (1),
.BR discipline (1)
